course: dictionary
lesson: 742
title: Batch: a group made or dealt with together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A batch is an amount of something made at one time, or a group of things dealt with together. A baker makes a batch of cookies in one go, and a teacher may check the next batch of spellings together. Batch can be a noun or a verb: to batch things means to put them into groups.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «A best-before date is about quality and a use-by date on fresh food is about safety; the batch number printed beside it lets a factory recall every packet from one bad batch.» Every packet comes from one group made together, so a batch must be a group of things made at one time.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «one bad group of packets made together» still makes sense, so your meaning fits. If it did not fit, you would try another meaning.
fact: A batch is an amount of something made at one time.
fact: A batch can also be a group of things or people dealt with together, such as the next batch of pupils.
fact: In maths, batches are equal groups: 4 batches of 12 cookies make 48 cookies.
fact: «One bad batch» means one group made together that has a fault, so a factory may recall every packet from it.
fact: Batch cooking means making lots of food at once to eat later.
exercise: What does batch cooking mean? | Cooking one small snack at a time | *Making lots of food at once to eat later | Burning food on purpose | Cooking only in the morning
exercise: «She bakes 4 batches of 12 cookies.» How many cookies does she bake altogether? | 12 | 16 | 42 | *48
exercise: «The factory checked each batch before the packets were sent out.» What is a batch in this sentence? | A delivery van | *A group of things made together | A single packet | A kind of machine
test: What does batch mean in «the next batch of pupils»? | A tiny cake | A bus ride | *A group of pupils dealt with together | A school bell
test: To batch things means to do what? | Throw them away | Hide them in a box | *Put them into groups to deal with together | Break them into pieces
exam: Which meaning fits batch in «a batch of letters»? | A single letter | A stamp | A postbox | *A group of letters dealt with together
